om/users/samdark/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samdark/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samdark/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/comments/376197684","html_url":"https://github.com/yiisoft/yii2/issues/14834#issuecomment-376197684","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/14834","id":376197684,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3NjE5NzY4NA==","user":{"login":"rugabarbo","id":6429469,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0Mjk0Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6429469?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo","html_url":"https://github.com/rugabarbo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-03-26T15:02:17Z","updated_at":"2018-03-26T15:02:17Z","body":"1) I just created PR that will allow to ignore 'TIMESTAMP' column definition test when `NO_ZERO_DATE` enabled (it's default for MySQL 5.7). \r\n\r\n2) It strange decision to use strictest mode for MySQL **5.6** test environment because strict mode reduces testing capabilities (for example, it isn't possible to test this 'TIMESTAMP' column definition case), and MySQL <= **5.6** doesn't use strict mode by default. It's good decision for MySQL **5.7** because it uses the strict mode by default: https://www.percona.com/blog/2016/10/18/upgrading-to-mysql-5-7-beware-of-the-new-strict-mode/\r\n\r\n3) However, if you want to use strictest mode you should enable `NO_ZERO_DATE` and `NO_ZERO_IN_DATE` in travis configuration together. I've never seen them turned on separately for MySQL instances. \r\n\r\n4) @rob006 you can't use `TIMESTAMP NULL` column definition without `DEFAULT` value (for MySQL). So if you want to call `null()` implicitly for `timestamp()` you also must call `defaultValue(null)` for it...","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/comments/376197684/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"rugabarbo","id":6429469,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0Mjk0Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6429469?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo","html_url":"https://github.com/rugabarbo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rugabarbo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":1541093716,"node_id":"MDE0Ok1lbnRpb25lZEV2ZW50MTU0MTA5MzcxNg==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/events/1541093716","actor":{"login":"rob006","id":5972388,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcj